 {
  "id": "Q-0026",
  "sourceId": "src_cc2f9b33d3",
  "text": "Feature Request: Project-Level PRD Generation and Phase/Status Tracking",
  "start": 0,
  "end": 71,
  "line": 1,
  "kind": "request",
  "intensity": 0.4,
  "customer": "cust_7f1890e6",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2025-10-25T23:51:54.000Z",
  "sha256": "6f45e66131eca375a2066d2afdc73687338ffaabe405238a9d3067e11890e84b",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0027",
  "sourceId": "src_cc2f9b33d3",
  "text": "In larger projects, it becomes difficult to track high-level progress, plan upcoming phases, or update the project status holistically.",
  "start": 379,
  "end": 514,
  "line": 4,
  "kind": "pain",
  "intensity": 0.5,
  "customer": "cust_7f1890e6",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2025-10-25T23:51:54.000Z",
  "sha256": "e8322326b69d92b7c73cdb644a5be5c789e1d38c58821a2c7aa4b293036e07ae",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0028",
  "sourceId": "src_cc2f9b33d3",
  "text": "Accept the *complete* project’s requirements and generate a structured PRD representing the full scope of the project, broken down by phases and sub-tasks.",
  "start": 837,
  "end": 992,
  "line": 9,
  "kind": "pain",
  "intensity": 0.5,
  "customer": "cust_7f1890e6",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2025-10-25T23:51:54.000Z",
  "sha256": "5930baecc95432eb26ee89b6c80bc54ba4261941ca9549b0030ef841eb4e39d9",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0029",
  "sourceId": "src_cc2f9b33d3",
  "text": "Workarounds include maintaining a separate document or external tracker, but these quickly become unsynchronized and lack the tight integration with Spec Kit’s existing workflow and automation.",
  "start": 1668,
  "end": 1861,
  "line": 18,
  "kind": "request",
  "intensity": 0.4,
  "customer": "cust_7f1890e6",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2025-10-25T23:51:54.000Z",
  "sha256": "67ee639465e66d4798708fdc8748eebb505ed6c98ed2440c599e7b3a8cbd48be",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0030",
  "sourceId": "src_f7290b0593",
  "text": "[Feature]: Standard evaluator contract for evidence, provenance, uncertainty, and recovery",
  "start": 0,
  "end": 90,
  "line": 1,
  "kind": "request",
  "intensity": 0.15,
  "customer": "cust_89fdb185",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2026-08-23T20:26:31.000Z",
  "sha256": "cf58c1b4d81f497063f512723583d424c8d3c6739a449de48516348681f77a40",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0031",
  "sourceId": "src_f7290b0593",
  "text": "A generic evaluator contract should be able to support provenance engines, security checks, formal verification, factuality systems, enterprise policy, deterministic linters, and future approaches.",
  "start": 3373,
  "end": 3570,
  "line": 79,
  "kind": "request",
  "intensity": 0.4,
  "customer": "cust_89fdb185",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2026-08-23T20:26:31.000Z",
  "sha256": "0a5991e0597bc46321c245062a171ca56998aedb14d32c143bfe4f1a57df7593",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0032",
  "sourceId": "src_f7290b0593",
  "text": "when evidence is insufficient, an evaluator should be able to request clarification, evidence gathering, abstention, escalation, iteration, or blocking rather than inventing certainty;",
  "start": 8394,
  "end": 8578,
  "line": 167,
  "kind": "pain",
  "intensity": 0.5,
  "customer": "cust_89fdb185",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2026-08-23T20:26:31.000Z",
  "sha256": "285de0456e9a10854a7280633061f1b013f0980034d1b260391686c819061ba2",
  "extractor": "heuristic"
 },
 {
  "id": "Q-0033",
  "sourceId": "src_f7290b0593",
  "text": "These are examples of policies that a generic evaluator contract should be able to express.",
  "start": 8806,
  "end": 8897,
  "line": 171,
  "kind": "request",
  "intensity": 0.4,
  "customer": "cust_89fdb185",
  "segment": "user",
  "date": "2026-08-23T20:26:31.000Z",
  "sha256": "0f64e9e364b7fab41a04b2b73549cbc0a760640c6b34bf6f7a890e78300c1a7f",
